// Project mode, the founder loop (docs/plan/11-project-mode.md section 5): plugins/jorah-projects.
// DRAFT: not applied. The install session (plan section 12, step 4) applies it on Adam's yes, after
// the runner is installed (the registry and /home/jorah/.jorah-projects exist) and after jorah-guard
// runs with a permission-matrix.json that has the project rules (grep '"project_set_level"').
//
// Also needed, not in this file:
//   - plugins.allow: the LIVE list plus "jorah-projects" (read it with
//     `openclaw --profile jorah config get plugins.allow`; never a fixed copy, as install-proactive.sh does).
//   - main's tool list: projects-tools.patch.json5 (read its header first).
//   - `openclaw --profile jorah plugins enable jorah-projects` from /opt/jorah/plugins/jorah-projects.
// The plugin needs no hooks.allowConversationAccess: it uses before_tool_call and message_received
// only (docs: plugins/hooks.md, "Permissions and scope").
//
// Paths: mediaRoots are where OpenClaw keeps attachments Adam sends. The docs give
// ~/.openclaw/media/inbound (channels/line.md) and a sandbox's media/inbound (gateway/config-agents/
// sandbox.md); Jorah's state dir is ~/.openclaw-jorah. CHECK ON THE PC before applying: send a photo
// to Jorah, then `ls -la /home/jorah/.openclaw-jorah/media/inbound /home/jorah/workspace/media/inbound`
// and fix this list to the folders that exist. Attachments seen arriving in the same chat are taken
// even outside these folders; any other path is refused.
//
// Dry run on the PC:
//   openclaw --profile jorah config patch --file /opt/jorah/config/pc/projects.patch.json5 --dry-run
// Expected: "Dry run successful" with plugins.entries.jorah-projects.{enabled,config}.
// Undo: `openclaw --profile jorah plugins disable jorah-projects`, then a patch with
// plugins.entries."jorah-projects": null and the allow list without it.
{
  plugins: {
    entries: {
      "jorah-projects": {
        enabled: true,
        config: {
          registryFile: "/home/jorah/.config/jorah-projects/projects.json",
          stateRoot: "/home/jorah/.jorah-projects",
          workRoot: "/home/jorah/work",
          guardStateDir: "/home/jorah/.jorah-guard",
          timeZone: "Europe/Bratislava",
          workspace: "/home/jorah/workspace",
          mediaRoots: ["/home/jorah/.openclaw-jorah/media/inbound", "/home/jorah/workspace/media/inbound"],
          gitBin: "/usr/bin/git",
          procRoot: "/proc",
          // Whose repos project_start and project_connect take (Adam's; the GitHub App's rulesets
          // cover them). The Mac command Jorah names for putting a local-only project on GitHub.
          githubOwners: ["AdamHikl"],
          newRepoScript: "scripts/github/new-project-repo.sh",
        },
      },
    },
  },
}
